# ADT multi-entry union declaration: [type [let a] [Ok a] [Error String]]
# registers a parameterized Union type alias with two NominalVariant constructors.
# At runtime, the type dict contains the constructor functions Ok and Error.
# Calling Ok with an integer and Error with a string both succeed.
[
  Result: [type [let a] [Ok a] [Error String]]
  ok-val:  [Ok 42]
  err-val: [Error "something went wrong"]
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Function(), "Error": Function()}), "ok-val": Variant(Result.Ok, Int(42)), "err-val": Variant(Result.Error, String("something went wrong"))})
